title: the_race
speaker: dm
---
<<map manor_drive>>
It's the first day of the celebration. The sun shines brightly down on Thistledown Manor in the cold autumn air. Someone has hung garlands and other decorations from every window. #line:race_first_day
A stone drive loops around a fountain in front of the house. A statue of a fish spits water into the basin of the fountain. Its nose shows the distinct signs of recent repairs. #line:race_fountain
Villagers line the hedges along the drive, not seeming to react much to the four "chariots" lined up at the start. Mostly these are just farm carts with the backs cut off and painted in sloppy bright colors. #line:race_chariots
Barnaby and Tobias are already standing between the shafts of one of the carts. They're wearing borrowed livery and Barnaby's barely fits. #line:race_livery
As you approach this cart you see GRIST on the side where the gold paint hasn't completely covered. Barnaby grumbles under his breath and glares at Tobias. Tobias just grins at you. #line:race_grist_cart
There are three more carts lined up alongside yours and the other three riders call out introductions. #line:race_riders
Sir Godfrey Bunting is a large man with two very nervous footmen waiting at his cart. #line:race_godfrey
Lady Prudence Kettle is being pulled by her gardener and his son, who don't seem surprised that she is knitting something. #line:race_prudence
Lionel Spratt has four men between the shafts of his cart. He clears his throat pointedly and one of the servants, with a start, informs you that Lionel is Lord Percival's nephew. #line:race_lionel
You and the other riders fall silent as a man steps up onto the stand, scroll in hand. The ring of keys at his belt jingles every time he moves. #line:race_steward
Tobias whispers to you that this is Amos Harker, the steward, who has keys for everything. #line:race_amos_whisper
All rise for His Lordship, the Honorable Lord Percival Thistledown. #line:race_all_rise #speaker:amos
The villagers are already standing and the nobles in the stands don't get up off the benches. #line:race_already_standing
Lord Percival climbs up on the stand, taking his time about it. His purple velvet clothing almost hides the thick chain of office around his neck. He lifts one gloved hand and looks out over the crowd. #line:race_percival_climbs
Amos starts clapping. Lord Percival smiles a bit wider. Clearly this is what he was waiting for. After a minute, the crowd claps as well. #line:race_clapping
My people. One year ago today, I came to you eager to make a difference. Today I am your lord, your benefactor, your friend. The bounty of Thistledown has never been greater! #line:race_speech_1 #speaker:lord_percival_thistledown
In honor of my first glorious year, I give you this week-long celebration. Let us partake of the festivities with the long-awaited chariot race. Three laps around the fountain. Begin! #line:race_speech_2 #speaker:lord_percival_thistledown
Amos lifts a lace handkerchief high in the air. He lets it drop, signaling the start of the race. Barnaby and Tobias lean in and the cart lurches forward. #line:race_start
<<jump race_lap_1>>
===
title: race_lap_1
speaker: dm
---
The cart bucks over the stone drive. The cart was designed for pulling grain and flour, not a rider. #line:race_lap1_bucks
-> Brace yourself and hold on tight. #line:race_lap1_opt_brace
    <<check athletics 12>>
-> Move with the cart and keep your balance. #line:race_lap1_opt_balance
    <<check acrobatics 12>>
<<if $passed>>
    <<set $race_passes to $race_passes + 1>>
    You brace yourself as the two men settle into a steady trot. Lady Prudence is still knitting as you pass by her. #line:race_lap1_pass
<<else>>
    The cart hits a rut. You land hard on your backside and scramble back up to see Lady Prudence passing you, still knitting. #line:race_lap1_fail
<<endif>>
<<jump race_lap_2>>
===
title: race_lap_2
speaker: dm
---
You pull up alongside Sir Godfrey. He sneers at you as he directs his servants to collide into your cart and calls out "Make way, peasant!" #line:race_lap2_godfrey
-> "Is that the king in the stands?" #line:race_lap2_opt_king
    <<check deception 12>>
    <<if $passed>>
        <<set $race_passes to $race_passes + 1>>
        Sir Godfrey looks at the crowd. His footmen slow down to look as well and you quickly leave them behind. #line:race_lap2_king_pass
    <<else>>
        Sir Godfrey scoffs at you as his cart hits yours. Barnaby and Tobias get you back on track just before you hit the fountain, but Sir Godfrey pulls ahead of you. #line:race_lap2_king_fail
    <<endif>>
-> Time it so Sir Godfrey's footmen miss your cart. #line:race_lap2_opt_timing
    <<check perception 12>>
    <<if $passed>>
        <<set $race_passes to $race_passes + 1>>
        You watch the footmen coming and slow down just in time. Sir Godfrey's cart flies across your path, just missing you. His men can't stop in time to avoid the fountain and he sails over the front of it and into the water. #line:race_lap2_timing_pass
    <<else>>
        Your timing is just a hair off and his cart clips yours. Barnaby and Tobias get you back on track just before you hit the fountain, but Sir Godfrey pulls ahead of you. #line:race_lap2_timing_fail
    <<endif>>
<<jump race_lap_3>>
===
title: race_lap_3
speaker: dm
---
Lionel Spratt is out in front. He's down to three men and you don't see any sign of the fourth. #line:race_lap3_lionel
As you come to the halfway point of this last lap, a pig goes squealing through the crowd with a kitchen helper in pursuit. #line:race_lap3_pig
Your cart slows considerably as Tobias stares at the pig. #line:race_lap3_slows
Her Royal Hoggness? #line:race_lap3_tobias #speaker:tobias
Tobias! Pull! PULL! #line:race_lap3_barnaby #speaker:barnaby
-> "Tobias! We'll get her back. Pull!" #line:race_lap3_opt_persuade
    <<check persuasion 12>>
-> Jump down and shake Tobias out of it. #line:race_lap3_opt_jump
    <<check acrobatics 12>>
<<if $passed>>
    <<set $race_passes to $race_passes + 1>>
    Tobias starts with a jerk and leans back into the shafts. You draw level with Lionel's cart and it's neck and neck to the finish line, neither of you gaining a significant lead. #line:race_lap3_pass
<<else>>
    Tobias stares at the pig for a long moment before he starts really pulling again. You catch up to Lionel's cart when the finish line is just ahead of you. #line:race_lap3_fail
<<endif>>
<<jump race_finish>>
===
title: race_finish
speaker: dm
---
<<if $race_passes >= 2>>
    <<set $race_won to true>>
    You pull ahead of Lionel at the last moment, crossing the finish line first, but just barely. #line:race_won_finish
    The crowd along the hedges cheers as Barnaby and Tobias slow to a stop, panting as they sit down right where they are. #line:race_won_cheer
    Lord Percival looks at you, then at the two men who pulled your "chariot" and decides to be gracious. #line:race_won_gracious
    A stranger! How marvelous! My guests shall be pleased. You shall sit at my table for the grand banquet. #line:race_won_percival #speaker:lord_percival_thistledown
    Uncle, it's not fair. Do you see the muscles on that blacksmith? #line:race_won_lionel #speaker:lionel
    Don't be tiresome, Lionel. #line:race_won_tiresome #speaker:lord_percival_thistledown
<<else>>
    <<set $race_lost to true>>
    Lionel pulls ahead of you at the last moment, crossing the finish line first, but just barely. #line:race_lost_finish
    The crowd along the hedges is mostly silent, but one or two applaud his win as Barnaby and Tobias slow to a stop, panting as they sit down right where they are. #line:race_lost_silent
    At least we have a backup plan. Kitchen help it is. #line:race_lost_backup #speaker:tobias
<<endif>>
The celebration continues for the rest of the week. From the village, you can hear music and laughter drifting down from the manor every night. #line:race_week
<<rest long>>
<<if $race_won>>
    <<jump banquet_guest>>
<<endif>>
<<jump banquet_kitchen>>
===
